;; The round trip's negative controls (doc/GATE-SURVEY.md, GTS81 (a), "As built: GT9's controls"; arbace.repr.cpp.rtcheck/controls): each is a
;; crossed pair of two files of the run, both passing the round trip: the :subject's print judged by every level's own comparison against
;; the :reference's original, which must differ at each level that has both sides (level 1 the forms again, level 3 the normalized AST dump,
;; level 4 each compiler's object, level 5 the :full print against the source). A control the comparison passes (the same at a level) or that
;; was compared at no level while its files were in the run fails the run; one whose files the run lacks (a list without them,
;; --no-objects for level 4's side) is left. No control is a row of results.tsv, the known file, the records or the counts. :subject
;; and :reference are names as the list writes them or as the known file qualifies them. Read with the Clojure reader.
[{:id "_control/bitfields-vs-io" :subject "samples/bitfields.cpp" :reference "samples/io.cpp"
  :why "samples 9 and 6: both pass all five levels; other declarations, other ASTs, other objects, other bytes"}]
